    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d142">

                <pb facs="0138" n="128" sameAs="frus:frus1944v04/pg128"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.20 Defense (M) Portugal/1534: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Minister in Portugal</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Norweb</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1944-06-07T16:00:00-04:00">June 7, 1944—4
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1645. This is an interim reply to your 1725, June 6. IPOC<anchor n="3"
                        xml:id="d142-f1"/> is meeting immediately to expedite supply purchase
                    arrangements. Pending detailed examination of data, general understanding of
                    Department and FEA is that approach will be liberal one as outlined in paragraph
                    5, our 132, January 17. We agree to extend period of program and to arrange for
                    supply of additional items such as locomotives, if possible on supply grounds.
                    Shipping question may pose serious difficulties if it should come to fore, but
                    we will press strongly should action be necessary. Incidentally, 100 jeeps will
                    be aboard next Portuguese ship. Sent to Lisbon, repeated to London.<anchor n="4"
                        xml:id="d142-f2"/>
                </p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d142-f1" n="3" xml:id="d142-f1-content">
                <p>Iberian Peninsular Operating Committee.</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d142-f2" n="4" xml:id="d142-f2-content">
                <p>Repeated to London as No. 4512.</p>
            </note>
